#### 2.5.2 Wang Model

In Wang's model [25], the MRS parameterization (previous version of MRST) for the PDFs, the BKK parameterization for the FFs, and the new HIJING parameterization [10] for the nuclear modification to the PDFs are used. The parton energy loss is calculated via a detailed balance theory [25]. The corresponding energy loss in a static medium with a uniform gluon density \(\rho_{0}\) over a distance \(R_{A}\) is \(dE_{0}/dL=(R_{A}/2\tau_{0})\langle dE/dL\rangle_{1d}\), where \(\langle dE/dL\rangle_{1d}\) is the average parton energy loss over the distance \(R_{A}\) in a 1-d Bjorken expanding medium with the initial gluon density \(\rho_{0}\); and an effective quark energy loss

